. Behavior kept:\n   - _try_rate_admit (orchestration.py:288) calls globals(), which after rebinding returns the facade dict, so it finds _plan088_rate_admit as in the base (base text identical at rc1 diff-16:2962-2970).\n   - _PLAN088_RATE_STATE and the _PLAN090_*_BUCKETS dicts are deep-copied into the facade, and the rebound functions mutate that copy. _plan088_rate_state_clear clears the same object.\n   - Default values (time.time, time.monotonic, 4096) are evaluated as in the base.\n   - iter_events reaches the rebound replay.iter_events through the SimpleNamespace at audit_emit.py:457-461, so patching _log_path still works.\n5. Base comparison:\n   - The regexes and bounds are byte-identical to the base: the review_id gate, the 12/16/64-hex gates, _PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_MS_MAX, the payload cap and the rate cap.\n   - 247 top-level defs were removed from audit_emit.py. Of those, emit_generic was rewritten in the facade, and the rest are in the parts.\n   - The odd blank lines in emit_audit_tokens_key_dropped are also in the base.\n6. The one semantic change in these files: _LEARNING_RAIL_ENUM gains bash_indirect, and _LEARNING_SWITCH_ENUM gains CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_GUARD and CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_HEURISTICS (lifecycle_schemas.py:508-516; base at rc1 diff-15:3198-3204). It is an additive closed enum, CHANGELOG.md:105 declares it, and its producer is bash_indirect_telemetry.py:59-60.\n7. Python 3.9, standard library only. The parts import re and time; install() uses copy, importlib and types. There is no syntax newer than 3.9. Annotations stay unevaluated strings under `from __future__ import annotations`. Deep-copying a compiled regex returns the same object (Python 3.7+).\n8. Fail direction. The emitters' logic is unchanged. The canonical_edit modules import audit_emit lazily, inside try blocks (utility.py:49 and :116, signature_rail.py:58-91, decisions.py:14), so an audit failure still fails open.\n9. Delivery and kernel. install.sh:1520-1550 copies every top-level _lib entry, subdirectories included. check_arbitration_kernel.py:312 carries `.claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/*` (condition 5).\n10. Already declared, not new: pair-rail-inputs-hash-manifest.txt:27 pins only audit_emit.py, not pair_rail.py and routing.py, where the emit_pair_rail_* code now lives. CHANGELOG.md:382-384 declares this in Known-open.\n\nDECLARED CONDITIONS: conditions 5 and 7 hold against this payload, and the enum part of condition 6 matches. Nothing in this payload makes any of conditions 1-14 or the GA-only conditions false.\n\nP0: none.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none at P1.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n\nP2-1. FILE:LINE: .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:12. The annotations involved are at rate_limits.py:268 and :279, orchestration.py:475 and :478, routing.py:386-390, tokens_boot.py:80-84 and :309-312, and replay.py:342-345.\n- What changed: the base facade imported Callable, Iterator, List and Tuple (rc1 diff-14:60). The candidate facade imports only Any, Dict and Optional.\n- Why it matters: the rebound functions resolve their string annotations in the facade's namespace, and install() merges the parts' module annotations into audit_emit.__annotations__.\n- Failure scenario: get_type_hints() on audit_emit.emit_pair_rail_codex_injection_detected, _plan088_rate_admit, iter_events or scrub_audit_tokens_event, or get_type_hints(audit_emit) itself, now raises NameError; it worked in the base. I found no production consumer: test_audit_emit.py:1567 imports get_type_hints but never calls it.\n- Minimal fix: put Callable, Iterator, List and Tuple back in the facade's typing import at the next kernel ceremony.\n\nP2-2. FILE:LINE: .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:460-461, with .claude/scripts/check-audit-read-api-stable.py:111-125.\n- What changed: the frozen read API iter_events now has the signature (*args, **kwargs) and is no longer a generator function (inspect.isgeneratorfunction returns False). Existing callers keep working.\n- Failure scenario: the freeze guard checks only the name, so a later rename of path or action_filter at replay.py:342 would pass it.\n- Minimal fix: give the facade wrapper the explicit signature (path=None, action_filter=None), or point the guard at replay.py.\n\nP2-3. Stale source-of-truth pointers left by the move:\n- .claude/governance/audit_tokens_allowlist.json:2-3 names `_lib/audit_emit.py:_AUDIT_TOKENS_ALLOWLIST` as the source of truth; it now lives at lifecycle_schemas.py:137.\n- SPEC/v1/soc2-control-map.schema.md:523-524 gives the verification method \"grep '^def emit_' .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py\". That now finds 2 emitters out of about 245; no script runs it, but someone following it by hand would conclude the emitters are missing.\n- docs/HONEST-LIMITATIONS.md:283.\n- Comments in pair_rail.py and routing.py still cite audit_emit.py line numbers (\"audit_emit.py:386-396\", \"line ~3484\").\n- Minimal fix: point all of these at _lib/audit_emit.py plus _lib/_audit_emit_parts/.","decision":"GO","sentence":"The 13 audit_emit parts in this payload match the base code, apart from one additive enum the CHANGELOG declares; every name they use resolves in the facade, they stay standard-library only, Python 3.9 compatible and fail-open, and they make no declared condition false and contain no P0 or new P1, only three P2 follow-ups."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":364,"cache_read_input_tokens":225605,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":364},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3d94731-802e-46e1-9fa0-3006a5880d2e","uuid":"09b36056-b730-47ea-9306-32f8343b3153","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:04:11.237Z","request_id":"req_011Ch73hnB3YWoJNKY5RMJwe","wire_tool_inputs":{"