s payload makes any of conditions 1-14 or the GA-only conditions false.\\n\\nP0: none.\\n\\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none at P1.\\n\\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\\n\\nP2-1. FILE:LINE: .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:12. The annotations involved are at rate_limits.py:268 and :279, orchestration.py:475 and :478, routing.py:386-390, tokens_boot.py:80-84 and :309-312, and replay.py:342-345.\\n- What changed: the base facade imported Callable, Iterator, List and Tuple (rc1 diff-14:60). The candidate facade imports only Any, Dict and Optional.\\n- Why it matters: the rebound functions resolve their string annotations in the facade's namespace, and install() merges the parts' module annotations into audit_emit.__annotations__.\\n- Failure scenario: get_type_hints() on audit_emit.emit_pair_rail_codex_injection_detected, _plan088_rate_admit, iter_events or scrub_audit_tokens_event, or get_type_hints(audit_emit) itself, now raises NameError; it worked in the base. I found no production consumer: test_audit_emit.py:1567 imports get_type_hints but never calls it.\\n- Minimal fix: put Callable, Iterator, List and Tuple back in the facade's typing import at the next kernel ceremony.\\n\\nP2-2. FILE:LINE: .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:460-461, with .claude/scripts/check-audit-read-api-stable.py:111-125.\\n- What changed: the frozen read API iter_events now has the signature (*args, **kwargs) and is no longer a generator function (inspect.isgeneratorfunction returns False). Existing callers keep working.\\n- Failure scenario: the freeze guard checks only the name, so a later rename of path or action_filter at replay.py:342 would pass it.\\n- Minimal fix: give the facade wrapper the explicit signature (path=None, action_filter=None), or point the guard at replay.py.\\n\\nP2-3. Stale source-of-truth pointers left by the move:\\n- .claude/governance/audit_tokens_allowlist.json:2-3 names `_lib/audit_emit.py:_AUDIT_TOKENS_ALLOWLIST` as the source of truth; it now lives at lifecycle_schemas.py:137.\\n- SPEC/v1/soc2-control-map.schema.md:523-524 gives the verification method \\\"grep '^def emit_' .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py\\\". That now finds 2 emitters out of about 245; no script runs it, but someone following it by hand would conclude the emitters are missing.\\n- docs/HONEST-LIMITATIONS.md:283.\\n- Comments in pair_rail.py and routing.py still cite audit_emit.py line numbers (\\\"audit_emit.py:386-396\\\", \\\"line ~3484\\\").\\n- Minimal fix: point all of these at _lib/audit_emit.py plus _lib/_audit_emit_parts/.\",\"decision\":\"GO\",\"sentence\":\"The 13 audit_emit parts in this payload match the base code, apart from one additive enum the CHANGELOG declares; every name they use resolves in the facade, they stay standard-library only, Python 3.9 compatible and fail-open, and they make no declared condition false and contain no P0 or new P1, only three P2 follow-ups.\"}","structured_output":{"report":"SCOPE: payload 3/34 adds 13 new files under .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/: lifecycle_schemas, operations, optimizer, orchestration, pair_rail, planning, rate_limits, replay, resource_events, routing, security, streaming and tokens_boot. They hold code moved out of the base _lib/audit_emit.py by PLAN-197. I checked them against the candidate tree, and against the base text kept in the committed rc1 evidence (the removed lines in diff-rc1-14/15/16.patch).\n\nWHAT I CHECKED\n1. Binding. install() (_audit_emit_parts/__init__.py:20-48) rebuilds each function with the facade's globals, so every free name in these files is looked up in audit_emit when the function runs. Each name resolves:\n   - emit_generic: audit_emit.py:473.\n   - _write_event, _breadcrumb, _log_path, _utc_now_iso: writer __all__.\n   - _scrub_ceo_boot_event: tokens_boot.\n   - _ATLAS_REGISTRY: adapters.py:314, a plain dict, so deepcopy works.\n   - _LEDGER_GATE_SIGNAL: harness_schemas.\n   - _ESTIMATE_DRIFT_* and _CEO_BOOT_TASK_CANDIDATE_EMITTED_ALLOWLIST: governance.\n   - _CEO_BOOT